  深宅大院 | shēn zhái dà yuàn | deep mansions and spacious courtyards; aristocratic compounds
  庭院深深 | tíng yuàn shēn shēn | courtyards deep and secluded; classical quietude
  安居乐业 | ān jū lè yè | live in peace and work with contentment
  和睦相处 | hé mù xiāng chǔ | live together in peaceful harmony

character_decomposition[3]{character,pinyin,meaning_en,meaning_es,radical,radical_meaning_en,meaning_component,sound_component,stroke_count,composition_type,etymology_and_mnemonic,visual_mnemonic_story_en,visual_mnemonic_story_es,tone_mnemonic_anchor,cangjie,traditional}:
  四 | sì | four; cardinal directions | cuatro; cuatro puntos cardinales | 囗 | enclosure | 囗 (four-sided enclosure) + 八 (diverging lines) | 四 (sì) | 5 | 全包围结构 | Enclosed box 囗 with two dividing lines inside; represents the four cardinal orientations: East, West, South, and North. | An enclosed space (囗) dividing cleanly into four cardinal quadrants (四). | Un recinto cerrado (囗) dividido en cuatro cuadrantes cardinales (四). | 51 | WC | 四
  合 | hé | join; enclose; unite; close | unir; juntar; cerrar; confluir | 人 | person | 人 (roof / covering lid) + 一 + 口 (box container) | 合 (hé) | 6 | 上下结构 | A lid 人 fitting seamlessly over a vessel 口; closing on all sides to form an enclosed harmonious unit. | Fitting a snug lid (人) onto a square box container (口) so four walls join seamlessly (合). | Ajustar una tapadera (人) sobre una caja (口) para que las cuatro paredes encajen en unión (合). | 35 | OMR | 合
  院 | yuàn | courtyard; compound; institution | patio; recinto; claustro | 阝 | mound / wall | 阝 (earthen boundary wall) + 完 (complete / whole) | 完 (wán / phonetic association) | 9 | 左右结构 | Boundary wall 阝 surrounding a completed domestic dwelling 完; a safe, open courtyard enclosed by perimeter walls. | Solid earthen perimeter walls (阝) sheltering a fully completed residential homestead (完): a peaceful courtyard (院). | Muros protectores (阝) que resguardan una vivienda entera y completa (完): el patio solariego (院). | 51 | NLJMU | 院

mnemonics_and_roots:
  composite_memory_hook_en: Four sides (四) joining in harmony (合) around an enclosed central courtyard (院) form a siheyuan (四合院).
  composite_memory_hook_es: Cuatro alas (四) cerradas en armonía (合) abrazando un patio interior (院) definen el siheyuan (四合院).
  cultural_and_cognitive_roots: Emblematic of ancient Chinese cosmological philosophy: square layout reflects 'round heaven and square earth' (天圆地方), fostering filial clan unity.
  tone_sandhi_and_pitch_modulation: Three syllables: 'sì hé yuàn' (51-35-51). Descend firmly on 'sì', rise smoothly on 'hé', and drop with resonance on 'yuàn'.

traps_and_cognates:
  look_alikes[4]{character,pinyin,meaning_en,distinction_note}:
    院 | yuàn | courtyard; institution | Mound radical 阝 on left of 完
    完 | wán | finish; complete | Roof 宀 over 元 without the 阝 radical
    合 | hé | join; close | Roof 人 over 一 and 口
    舍 | shè/shě | cottage; abandon | Has 舌-like structure below 𠆢
  etymological_cognates[4]{character,pinyin,gloss_en}:
