semantic_boundary_contrasts:
  core_nuance: 四合院 specifically denotes the quadrangle courtyard residential architecture of northern China.
  contrasts[3]{id,compared_word,pinyin,analysis}:
    1 | 四合院 vs. 公寓 | gōngyù | 公寓 designates modern multi-story apartment complexes with elevator lobbies, whereas 四合院 is a single-story walled inward-facing courtyard.
    2 | 四合院 vs. 别墅 | biéshù | 别墅 is a standalone suburban villa surrounded by open lawns, while 四合院 encloses an internal private courtyard hidden behind high outer walls.
    3 | 四合院 vs. 窑洞 | yáodòng | 窑洞 refers to cave dwellings carved into Loess Plateau bluffs in northwestern China, distinct from masonry 四合院.

extended_reading_passages[2]{id,hanzi,pinyin,en,es}:
  #1 | 四合院是中国华北地区最为典型的民居建筑形式。所谓四合，‘四’指东、西、南、北四面房屋，‘合’则是四面房屋围在一起，中间形成一个宽敞的方形院落。这种建筑布局既保证了家族起居的私密，又充满了人伦温情。 | Sìhéyuàn shì Zhōngguó Huáběi dìqū zuìwéi diǎnxíng de mínjū jiànzhù xíngshì. Suǒwèi sìhé, 'sì' zhǐ dōng, xī, nán, běi sì miàn fángwū, 'hé' zé shì sì miàn fángwū wéi zài yìqǐ, zhōngjiān xíngchéng yí ge kuānchǎng de fāngxíng yuànluò. Zhè zhǒng jiànzhù bùjú jì bǎozhèng le jiāzú qǐjū de sīmì, yòu chōngmǎn le rénlún wēnqíng. | The siheyuan is the most typical traditional residence in North China. 'Four' refers to the houses on four sides, while 'join' means enclosing them to form a spacious central square courtyard. This layout secures domestic privacy while brimming with clan warmth. | El siheyuan es la vivienda tradicional más emblemática del norte de China. Las cuatro alas en los puntos cardinales abrazan un amplio patio cuadrado central, resguardando la intimidad familiar y albergando un entrañable calor de hogar.
  #2 | 大户人家的四合院通常由好几座并列组成，院落之间往往有曲折的长廊相通。院内不仅种植着玉兰与海棠，还会摆放几口大水缸饲养金鱼。关起门来，四合院就是一个自成天地的独立世界；打开院门，邻里之间推心置腹，洋溢着极其浓郁的人情味。 | Dàhù rénjiā de sìhéyuàn tōngcháng yóu hǎojǐ zuò bìngliè zǔchéng, yuànluò zhījiān wǎngwǎng yǒu qūzhé de chángláng xiāngtōng. Yuànnèi bùjǐn zhòngzhí zhe yùlán yǔ hǎitáng, hái huì bǎifàng jǐ kǒu dà shuǐgāng sìyǎng jīnyú. Guān qǐ mén lái, sìhéyuàn jiùshì yí ge zìchéng-tiāndì de dúlì shìjiè; dǎkāi yuànmén, línlǐ zhījiān tuīxīn-zhìfù, yángyì zhe jíqí nóngyù de rénqíngwèi. | Wealthy siheyuan compounds comprised multiple courtyards side by side linked by winding verandas. Magnolias and crabapples flourished while ceramic vats held goldfish. Closed doors created a private haven; opened doors fostered neighborly warmth. | Las familias nobles alzaban varios patios yuxtapuestos enlazados por galerías. Plantaban magnolias y criaban peces de colores en tinajas. A puerta cerrada era un remanso íntimo; de par en par, emanaba una entrañable cordialidad vecinal.
